WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.380
A merchant's fee is rarely one number.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.035
This plan is 30 cents, plus 2.9 percent, plus a bundle of add-ons.

3
00:00:10.035 --> 00:00:13.984
And the bundle has rules of its own: here, 5 cents more.

4
00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.743
So some parts are single rules, and some are groups of rules.

5
00:00:17.743 --> 00:00:19.853
A group can even hold another group.

6
00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:23.957
The code that prices a payment should not have to care which is which.

7
00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.661
Draw the plan as a tree.

8
00:00:25.661 --> 00:00:30.768
The leaves are single rules: Flat for a fixed amount, and Percent in basis points.

9
00:00:30.768 --> 00:00:35.003
Each group is an AllOf, and the whole plan is one AllOf at the root.

10
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:39.506
Now ask the root one question: what is your fee on this payment?

11
00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:42.777
Say the payment is 100.00, which is 10,000 cents.

12
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.577
A group does not know the answer by itself.

13
00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:50.672
It passes the same question on to each child, and the inner group passes it on again.

14
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:52.891
Leaves answer directly.

15
00:00:52.891 --> 00:00:54.036
Flat says 30.

16
00:00:54.036 --> 00:00:57.556
Percent says 2.9 percent of 10,000: 290.

17
00:00:57.556 --> 00:01:00.813
Down in the inner group, Flat says 5.

18
00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:02.893
So what does the root return?

19
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:08.739
Each group adds up what its children return.

20
00:01:08.739 --> 00:01:11.027
The inner group returns 5.

21
00:01:11.027 --> 00:01:15.340
The root returns 30, plus 290, plus 5: 325 cents.

22
00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:17.411
That is the Composite pattern.

23
00:01:17.411 --> 00:01:20.604
A group and a single rule answer the same question.

24
00:01:20.604 --> 00:01:26.113
So the caller asks the root, and never checks whether it holds one rule or a whole tree.

25
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:30.174
In code, one recursive function prices any plan.

26
00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:32.333
It has one case per kind of node.

27
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:37.763
The AllOf case calls fee again on each child: that call is the arrow down the tree.

28
00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:39.959
The switch has no default branch.

29
00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:45.115
Add a new kind of node, and the compiler flags every switch that does not handle it.

30
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:53.833
The rule: a group answers by asking its children and adding up, so one recursive function prices a tree of any depth.

31
00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.019
A quick check.

32
00:01:55.019 --> 00:01:59.302
The inner group gets a second rule: Percent of 50 basis points.

33
00:01:59.302 --> 00:02:02.769
For the same 100.00, what does the root return now?
